hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Knowledge will be taken away, tribulations will appear, and killing will become widespread."" We asked him: What is killing? He (peace be upon him) said: ""Killing."" When Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) heard the statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Knowledge will be taken away,"" he said: ""The disappearance of knowledge does not mean that it will be taken out from the hearts of the people, rather the ending of knowledge is due to the passing away of the scholars."""
"2","Ja'far narrated from this chain a similar narration, and he said: «فناء العلماء» (the disappearance of the scholars)."
"3","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""A time will come upon the people when they will narrate to you such ahadith that neither you nor your forefathers have heard, so avoid those people and those narrations."""
"4","Ka'b narrated: Some people will come who will adorn their words with falsehood; they will be called the companions of the tablets. The pearl will be separated from the gem."
"5","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever attributes to me something which I have not said, let him take his place in Hell. Whoever is consulted by his Muslim brother and does not give him sincere advice, then he has betrayed him. And whoever gives a fatwa without proper investigation, then its sin is upon the one who gave the fatwa."""
"6","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""Whoever gives a fatwa without knowledge, then its sin is upon the one who gave the fatwa."""
"7","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Sitting with people who supplicate to Allah and remember Him from the Fajr prayer until sunrise is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves from among the descendants of Isma'il, or that I free their like from Asr until sunset."""
"8","Sufyan bin Abdul Malik narrated: When Ibn al-Mubarak (may Allah have mercy on him) mentioned this hadith and some among them denied it, he said: These evil people will prevent us from abandoning the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and from narrating it. Should we abandon any hadith whose meaning we do not know? No, rather we will narrate it just as we have heard it, and we will blame our own selves for ignorance."
"9","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from four things: from knowledge that is of no benefit, from a heart that does not fear, from a soul that is not satisfied, and from a supplication that is not answered."""
"10","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for someone, He grants him understanding in the religion."""
"11","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""People are like mines of gold and silver in regard to good and evil. So those among them who were the best in the days of ignorance are the best among them in Islam, provided they gain understanding in the religion."""
"12","Shahr bin Hawshab narrated: Surah Al-An'am was revealed, and with it there was the loud voice of angels; they had filled the space from the sky of the world to the earth. He said: It is a Makki surah, except for its two verses: verse « قُلْ تَعَالَوْا أَتْلُ مَا حَرَّمَ رَبُّكُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ أَلَّا تُشْرِكُوا بِهِ شَيْئًا وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ إِحْسَانًا وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا أَوْلَادَكُم مِّنْ إِمْلَاقٍ نَّحْنُ نَرْزُقُكُمْ وَإِيَّاهُمْ وَلَا تَقْرَبُوا الْفَوَاحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا النَّفْسَ الَّتِي حَرَّمَ اللَّـهُ إِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ذَلِكُمْ وَصَّاكُم بِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ » and verse « وَلَا تَقْرَبُوا مَالَ الْيَتِيمِ إِلَّا بِالَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ أَشُدَّهُ وَأَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَالْمِيزَانَ بِالْقِسْطِ لَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا إِلَّا وُسْعَهَا وَإِذَا قُلْتُمْ فَاعْدِلُوا وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبَى وَبِعَهْدِ اللَّـهِ أَوْفُوا ذَلِكُمْ وَصَّاكُم بِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُونَ » ."
"13","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he recited this (verse of Surah Hud: 46) « عَمَلٌ غَيْرُ صَالِحٍ » in this way « عَمَلَ غَيْرُ صَالِحٍ » : ""He did not do righteous deeds."""
"14","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reciting (the verse from Surah Az-Zumar) « قُلْ يَا عِبَادِيَ الَّذِينَ أَسْرَفُوا عَلَى أَنفُسِهِمْ لَا تَقْنَطُوا مِن رَّحْمَةِ اللَّـهِ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا . . . ( وَلَا يُبَالِيْ ) إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ » [39-الزمر:59] (that is, I heard him reciting the word « وَلَا يُبَالِيْ » )."
"15","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reciting « إِنَّهُ عَمِلَ غَيْرَ صَالِحٍ » ."
"16","It is narrated from Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) that she asked regarding this (verse 46 of Surah Hud): so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: « إِنَّهُ عَمِلَ غَيْرَ صَالِحٍ » ."
"17","Syedna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrated: We used to memorize hadith only from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), but when you started walking on hard and soft ground, then (trusting you) is a far-fetched matter."
"18","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports in a marfu‘ narration that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There are two greedy ones, the greed of neither of them ends: the one who is greedy for seeking knowledge, his greed does not end; and the one who is greedy for seeking wealth, his greed also does not end.”"
"19","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: Whatever practice the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) established, I know it, and I do not know whether he used to recite (Qira’ah) in Zuhr and Asr or not. And I do not know whether he used to recite this « وَقَدْ بَلَغْتُ مِنَ الْكِبَرِ عِتِيًّا اَوْ عِسِيَّا » [19-مريم:8] — I have forgotten the third thing."
